{
  "$schema": "stdlib-conformances.schema.json",
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "comment": "Swift standard-library conformance facts the generator cannot recover from a local TypeDecl (the stdlib has no TypeDecl in the corpus). ONE input to ConformanceOracle, not the whole base: foreign cross-module conformances resolve via ABI-confirmed specialization hints and transitive refinement, not this table. A curated MATRIX: the type keys are the stdlib types the oracle answers for, `protocols` is the protocol axis it answers about, and each entry is exactly the axis protocols the live stdlib declares for that type. Do not hand-edit entries: to add a type, add its key with an empty list; to add a protocol, add it to `protocols`; then run `nuke regen-stdlib-conformances`, which reconciles every entry with a swift-api-digester dump of the live stdlib (pruning what it does not declare, completing what it does). Bump schemaVersion here AND ConformanceOracle.ExpectedStdlibSchemaVersion in lockstep on any shape change.",
